// THE GREAT SPECIES RENAME. I'm overwriting the names of (almost) every species, and giving fresh, new descriptions to each. With any luck, this won't explode people's characters or imports.

// HUMANOIDS START

/datum/species/human/northern
	name = "Humen"
	base_name = "Humenity"
	sub_name = "Humen"
	desc = "Humens (or \"Humans\") are the eldest of the Weeping God's creations. Noted for their \
	tenacity and overwhelming population, humens are the most commonly seen race across the lands, \
	at a rate of about ten to one in regions such as Grenzelhoft. However, to the west \
	the opposite is true. Humens come from a vast swathe of cultures and ethnicities, most of which \
	have historically been at odds with one another. Being the eldest creations of the Weeping God, humens \
	tend to find fortune easier than the other races, and are so diverse that no other racial traits \
	are dominant in their species."

/datum/species/demihuman
	name = "Halfblood"
	base_name = "Humenity"
	desc_title = "Halfblood"
	desc = "Product of cross-species breeding, otherworldly interference, or thaumaturgic channeling, a Halfblood has no singular definition; it is simply a catch-all term for any humanoid hybridized with animalistic traits. \n \n\
	Halfbloods are astoundingly abundant across the Known World - sired anywhere where humens, elves, orcs, or dwarves intersect with the wildblooded races; be they Landlocked, Seaborne, or Avian. \
	This commonality is ancient - recognized even during the times of ancient PSYDON - and has created such long, enduring lineages that countless noble houses are fully composed of the Halved outright. \n \n\
	A Halfblood’s species is typically obvious on initial inspection; a pair of feline ears, a crest of ram horns, a pair of avian or reptilian wings, so on and so forth. \
	Typically, individuals with a certain species’ traits can be identified with a common name - a goat-like kin may be identified as a \"Caprini,\" a rabbitblood a \"Lagomara,\" a bearblood \"Ursar,\" and a catblood may be called a \"Felin\", \"Felinid,\" or simply a \"catgirl.\" \n \n\
	Many bear behaviors of their originating species- ambition, wanderlust, pack dynamics, or affinities for the sea and sky, to name a few. These traits serve as a blessing or curse, depending on the individual; a half-fox’s venardine wit and quickness may just as well be key to her success - or cause her to meet a terrible end."

/datum/species/human/halfelf
	name = "Half-Elf"
	base_name = "Humenity"
	desc_title = "Half Elf"
	desc = "The child of an Elf and Humen, Half-Elves are generally frowned \
	upon by the more conservatively minded. \
	From physical to cultural characteristics, Half-Elves are an incredibly diverse people, \
	thanks in no small part to the incredibly varied nature of their Humen halves. Indeed, no other race \
	embodies the term \"melting pot\" quite like the Half-Elves. Due to their half-breed nature, their physical \
	characteristics can be either more Elvish or more Humen, depending on which of their parents' genes \
	are more predominant. In terms of cultural identity, a Half-Elf will typically choose to lean more \
	towards either their Humen or Elvish heritages."


// HUMANOIDS END

// BEAST SPECIES START
/datum/species/anthromorph
	name = "Wildblood"
	id = "anthromorph"
	base_name = "Beastbloods"
	desc_title = "Wildblood"
	desc = "The Known World, while predominantly populated by the Psydonic races - humens, elves, and dwarves - is a vast, fascinating ecosystem, and bears a countless variety of fine fruit, no matter how few there are. \
	While wildblooded species such as Lupians, Tabaxi, and the reptilian races are the most numerous, countless smaller, less widespread animalistic species exist. \n \n\
	Wildbloods is a catch-all term used to describe these minor races; though it is incapable of capturing the sheer breadth of variety in sentient life found across the World. A Wildblood may be completely unique; formed through alchemical, divine, or esoteric meddling, or part of long-enduring, tribal race on the fringes of society; the story always varies, and is often remarkably complex. \n \n\
	From land, sea, and air come these creatures; the Aari Aves from the chain of Jusaari, the sturdy Minotaurs, the amphibious Crustacrid culinary masters, the boorish Swine tribes of Gronn, the blood-craving Anophelii, and countless other species of rare, exotic existence. \
	Each bear their own anatomies, mentalities, histories, and commonalities- almost no two species of the Wild are alike. \n \n\
	Though some of these creatures could be the direct product of the Divine Wills, the sheer diversity of these species speaks to an innate, exceptional property of the world. \n \n\
	<i>Things that ought to crawl have learned to walk- then, they learned to talk, as well.</i>"


/datum/species/lupian
	base_name = "Beastbloods"
	desc = "Wolves among men. \n \n\
	The Lupian is a breed of bipedal canids known well across the world. With a stocky stature similar to that of the Orc - taller and broader than most humanoids - they lay ancestral claim to the lands arching northwest from Hammerhold; a bloody, distemperate land of fjords and frigid taiga best survived by the tight-knit packs of wolfmen across its once-unified frontier. \n \n\
	Having long spread scattershot to warmer climes as seafaring conquerors or mercenary warwolves for hire, Lupians are among the most common beastblooded races across the Known World, alongside Tabaxi. \
	Regular as they may be, however, outside of the North, most Lupians are considered through the cruelties of their shattered homeland: insular savages, tools of violence, and wolves at the gate. \n \n\
	To the pragmatic, they have their uses - capable, proud, and strong, but blades easily incited to violence."

/datum/species/moth
	base_name = "Beastbloods"
/datum/species/anthromorphsmall
	base_name = "Beastbloods"
	desc = "Verminvolk are primarily denoted from other wildblooded species simply by their diminutive stature - and being of a species that demands it. \n \n\
	Most typically, Verminvolk are rodents, marsupials, or rabbits of some manner or another - fast-breeding, fast-living species that, by way of their seedy stigma, often are pushed on the outskirts of society. \
	Like the lowly kobold or goblin, many Verminvolk are readily prejudiced against, especially within the Midderland - often regarded as being thieves, blasphemers, or grave-robbers- and easily put to blame for any wrong that falls upon a township. \n \n\
	To little surprise given their nature, Verminvolk have a strong taste for dairy and other fermented milk products. This, at least, provides many with legitimate work - and acceptance, hard-fought. \
	Those of the common species may disdain the Verminvolk, but they love their cheeses. Sharp or soft, goat or cow, aged or fresh, salted or sweet- such products sell well enough that these guilds often form the bedrock to any settled population of the Verm. \n \n\
	Dedicated cheesemaking guilds vary across population centers; each with their own specific method to ferment, mix, spice, and ripen their own unique product. These guilds are fiercely protective of their secrets- and, similar to that of Otavais vineyards, more than one soul too curious has vanished mysteriously after investigating a reclusive workshop."

/datum/species/tabaxi
	base_name = "Beastbloods"
/datum/species/vulpkanin
	base_name = "Beastbloods"
	desc = "Relative cousins to the Lupians of the North, the Venardine are a nomadic peoples spread scattershot around the Known World. Often travelling across countries and continents in migratory packs, the Venardine almost never settle in one place; establishing basal burrows on the fringes of society, plying their trade, then moving on when time - or trouble - demands they upend themselves. \n \n\
	Each time, they pluck elements from each culture their pack passes through- a Venard’s performance on stage might mix Midderland and Raneshan religious figures, or import lessons from Kazengun philosophies into a tale for young pups. Uniquely, Venardine are remarkably canny polyglots; quick to learn new languages in word and in writing. \
	A Venard translator is seen as a safe investment for many in a foreign land, though usually at the cost of a few tricks or amusing mistranslations. A tutor even more- literacy rates rise around where a caravan makes its stop in a mutually beneficial arrangement. \n \n\ Villagers learn their letters, the caravan is fed in exchange, and old grandmother vixens teach tales of old glories and lessons from long ago. \n \n\
	Still, though- most know them for their unconventional, libertine nature towards art, music, intimacy, and property. \
	This way of life is most commonly described as <i>\"Bohevriaan,\"</i> and has charmed poets, performers, and lured countless students of higher learning into lackadaisical dismissals of their duties."

// BEAST SPECIES END

// LIZARD PEOPLE START

/datum/species/lizardfolk
	name = "Eskallian"
	base_name = "Coldbloods"
	desc_title = "Eskallian"
	desc = "The Eskallian are semi-aquatic reptilian humanoids. \
	Their flesh is covered in scales varying in color from dark green to shades of brown and gray. \
	Taller than humans and powerfully built, Eskallian are often between 6 and 7 feet tall, bound with \
	semi-prehensile muscular tails that grow to three or four feet in length. \
	Ostensibly used for balance, these limbs are used as points of pride for any scaled culture."

/datum/species/kobold
	base_name = "Coldbloods"
	desc_title = "Kobold"
	desc = "Diminutive, slinking reptilians; cousins to the Eskallian, slaves to the Drakian. By escape or by exchange, Kobolds have spread widely into the Midderland from the spiderwebbing burrows buried beneath Lirvas - and are here to stay. \n \n\
	Liberated, kobolds can be quite talkative- which, when combined with their general lack of literacy and ad-hoc pidgin vernacular formed in the mines, regularly leads to a point of irritation for larger species."

/datum/species/dracon
	base_name = "Coldbloods"
	desc_title = "Drakian"
	desc = "Bearers of the draconic blood, the Drakian are a breed of imperious, thickly-scaled individuals defined best by their regal, reptilian bearing– and their great, sweeping wings. \
	Bipedal descendants of the True Dragons, they are a rarer species across the Known World: most of their population is found within the mountainous ranges of Lirvas. \n \n\
	Naturally blessed with surprising longevity by their blood, certain individuals have been known to live well past six hundred years. \
	Drakians are proud, ambitious, and high-blooded creatures; seeking success and societal ascension at any cost; to mild success within the Midderland. \n \n\
	<i>You will know a Drakian when you see one; if not, they will be more than happy to boast about it.</i>"

/datum/species/akula
	name = "Axian"
	base_name = "Coldbloods"
	desc_title = "Axian"
	desc = "Spreading outwards from the Eastern oceans, the Axians are a rare example of an amphibious Seaborne species - and, perhaps, their most common example upon the land. \
	Few do not recognize the characteristics of the Charcharodon - roughshod scales, serrative teeth, and an imposing stature more than suitable for protracted swims. \n \n\
	Due to their penchant for trade and travel, they can be found all over the world, oftentimes \
	seeing places many could not even dream of. They look down at those they considered the 'settled' \
	and often uproot themselves quite often in their lifetimes. However, due to the isolation upon the soils, many Axians \
	find their sanity being clawed away as they find themselves stuck in one place. \n \n\
	Of note with Axians is their unusual moral compass, especially those fresh out of water. Whereas slavery in all forms may be completely unacceptable to an Axian - such as those from the Marina - cannibalism of other individuals, particularly of those deemed 'lesser' is perfectly tolerable. \
	Slavery, in contrast, is viewed as the theft of choice and freedom; key to swimming along the shores - whereas the hunt and consumption of fellow Seaborne is commonplace and expected; especially after death. \n \n\
	Traditionally, Axians consume their dead as part of their funeral practices; better them than a Crustacrid or other bottom-feeding species. Certain species are even seen as delicacies - the peaceful Seal-Kin along the chain of Jusaari are often victim to Axiv hunts. \
	This practice has been quickly deemed anathematic by land-dwelling jurisdictions and temples- for obvious reasons."

// LIZARD SPECIES END

// GODTOUCHED START

/datum/species/aasimar
	desc = "Beings brought to life by the direct touch of the Divine Wills, the Aasimar are a rare peoples scattered across the world; each an example of the Miracle made manifest. \n \n\
	Shaped in the ideal, Divine vision of humanity - being taller and bearing an uncanny beauty - Aasimar are not born, but crafted- as holy golems, in a fashion; weaved into existence across the world by the thread of Life. \
	Their emergence is sublime - a whisper on the winds, a forge’s flame igniting without kindling, or a religious icon emerging from a mosaic or a venerable statue coming to life; marble made motile. Thus, a new being enters this world. \n \n\
	The making of these Crafts tend to vary: some are animate, marble statues - as is the <i>Kept-of-Stone</i> craft - whereas others, like those of <i>Swept-of-Wing,</i> are otherwise humanoid - but bear blessed wings upon their back. \
	Innate conduits to the Divines, they often find themselves as agents of the Temple; its guardians, scholars, and priesthood caste. \n \n\
	Regardless of their nature, Aasimar blood glitters golden when spilled. \n<i>It is a grave omen to any of the Faithful when the streets shine with threads of liquid gold.</i>"

/datum/species/tieberian
	desc = "Found roaming across the expansive landmasses of the Western Realms, Tieflings are some of the youngest species of the Known World. All Tieflings are half-kins, of sorts – scions of the city-states of Tlifchital, which long had normalized, venerated, and mastered the arcanist art of summoning the Daeva- burning beings temporarily realized from a realm esoteric. \n \n\
	Through ritualistic assimilation, these hybrids of worldly mortal and otherworldly Daevic were created; first marked by scarlet skin, cloven hooves, and prominent horns. \n \n\
	Such traits - and others like them - have carried over through eleven generations, if counted scholastically- and the city-states, ever curious, continue to create more. \n \n\
	East of the Realms, tieflings exist on the boundaries of societies; historically scorned or shunned by way of their birth. Originally, Pantheonic doctrine dictated them as unnatural abominations; their creation a blasphemy before the Pentacle. Though the Temple’s official perspective has eased since, only recently have such prejudices begun to fade across its peoples. "

// GODTOUCHED END

// ORCS & GOBS START

/datum/species/halforc
	name = "Orc"
	origin_default = /datum/virtue/origin/gronn
	origin = "Gronn"
	base_name = "Orkhors"
	desc_title = "Orc"
	desc = "Tusked, sturdy creatures sourced from Gronnic grasslands. Orcs are a people oft known and feared among the Midderland and Western Realms for their relentless raids, tribal customs, and commonplace, cultural practice of Graggaronn belief. \
	Diasporatic by way of trade, raid, or enslavement, Orcs are found all across the world - plying their often bloody trade in a world regularly trained to scorn them. \n \n\
	Regardless of their heritage as full-blooded or not, the word ‘half-orc’ is an intentional, denigratory exonym by the peoples of the Midlands: describing an orc that can live within the boundaries of the ‘civilized’ peoples."

/datum/species/goblinp
	name = "Goblin"
	base_name = "Orkhors"
	desc = "Scourge of villages, nuisance to townships, oddities all around, goblins are a fast-breeding, short-lived assortment of creatures found all across the Known World. \
	Typically, tribes can be found within burrows, caves, or the abundance of tunnels found below cities. Though universally short and generally of a greenish hue, goblins are uniquely varied– almost no other sapient species has more bizarrely diverse morphologies. \n \n\
	Individuals can range from gaunt, vicious, cruel cretins - with simplified anatomies as though a homunculus - to more thickly-set, intelligent individuals- closer in structure to an verdant-skinned humanoid, or perhaps a beardless dwarf. \n \n\
	With widespread tribal belief in Graggar, little inhibition towards their base impulses, and a careless disregard for almost anyone outside of their tribes, goblins are rarely accepted within society at large. To the ‘Tallones,’ goblins are seen as lesser beings at best, and active threats at worst. \
	The exception is within Gronn, where tribes freely cohabitate with orcs; viewed as their smaller, stranger cousins. \n \n\
	<i>Outcast, curiosity, or abuser: such is the lot of the grottinoid life.</i>"

// ORCS & GOBS END (primals soon!)

// ARTIFICIAL RACES

/datum/species/construct/metal
	name = "Metal Construct"
	id = "constructm"
	origin_default = /datum/virtue/origin/naledi
	origin = "Naledi"
	base_name = "Artificials"
	is_subrace = TRUE
	desc_title = "Metallic Construct"
	desc = "Masterworks of artifice, metal constructs are as the name implies- entirely constructed by mortal hands. They are beings not of flesh and blood, but cold metal and the arcyne. \
	Constructs are said to originate from works of Zizo, and they hail from the far-off lands of the Southern Empty- a great city of artifice, where the only artificers capable of understanding what is necessary to create the constructs live. \
	For some reason, they have found themselves travelling out of the empty, as of late. Children of the Resonator Siphon."

/datum/species/ooze
	name = "Murkling"
	id = "ooze"
	desc_title = "Murkling"
	base_name = "Artificials"
	desc = "Few know the true origins of the Murklings. Ancient records place their beginnings deep within the cold caverns of the Underdark \
	where primordial ooze infested tunnels and defended its spawning pits with relentless hostility. \n \n\
	For centuries, Dark Elves and Dwarven delvers alike sealed these regions away, leaving the living mire undisturbed. \
	Only within the last century did the ooze begin to change. \
	What emerged were crude humanoid figures that were somehow sentient. \
	They now stood in the shape of humens, two-legged, speaking, and curious to an unsettling degree. Once mindless sludge, they had become something new. \n \n\
	As their spawning pools withered like parents releasing their young, the Murklings formed colonies of their own. \
	Though hardened by the violent depths, they remain volatile and naive, struggling to understand a surface world that often sees them as monsters. \
	True to their nature, Murklings rapidly adapt to their surroundings, their forms shifting to match the lands they inhabit. \
	Yet this adaptability carries a curse: their bodies absorb more than shape. \n \n\
	Dusts, spirits, and smoke can alter them beyond recovery - breeding a severe dependence, \
	having consumed enough for their bodies to recreate and secrete the very substance that sustains them. \
	Caught now in the struggles of surface faiths and kingdoms, Murklings search for purpose beyond their primordial mothers. \
	Some turn to gods as they are susceptible to faith to fill the gaps their spawning pools left, and others reject them entirely. \
	Yet all carry the memory of the deep: the silent, all-encompassing love and will from which they were born."

